<section class="boundary"><div class="container"><h2>Important Information</h2><p>LegalDIY provides general legal education and self-help information about civil divorce in Malaysia. LegalDIY is not a law firm and does not represent individuals in legal proceedings.</p><p>The Joint Petition Knowledge Centre helps spouses understand issues they may need to consider when thinking about proceeding together. It does not determine whether Joint Petition is legally suitable, whether a proposed arrangement will be accepted by the court, or what legal outcome a person will receive.</p><p>Legal requirements and court procedures may change. Where you cannot proceed together, do not understand your rights, cannot make decisions freely, or have substantial disputed or complex issues, consider independent advice from a qualified legal professional.</p></div></section>
